<title>SWITZERLAND: Roche deal may dilute earnings.</title>
<headline>Roche deal may dilute earnings.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Roche Holding AG said that it expected a dilution in its earnings in the first year of its planned acquistion of Boehringer Mannheim.</p>
<p>This will not only be due to the cost of combining the two businesses, but also due to the fact that the transaction will be financed with liquid funds, some of which are yielding high returns.</p>
<p>Chief financial officer Henri Meier also said that the method of financing the transaction will depend to a large degree on the timing of the takeover, and the conditions in financial markets at that time.</p>
<p>&quot;We will probably take a bridging loan,&quot; Meier said, adding today's nominally low interest rates make such a credit attractive.</p>
</text>
